      "sha": "ae4dc210a936ee5500684f66dbfdc2f45523020e",
      "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/jphacks/tkb_2615/git/trees/ae4dc210a936ee5500684f66dbfdc2f45523020e"
    },
    "message": "Move staff_dynamics_v1 and the rules of domain/staff_dynamics.py to Rust\n\nRust owns the namespace in a typed row. update_staff_dynamics, the two availability readers,\nadd_staff, create_staff_dynamics_state, the canonical config and the shift-window override all run\nas kernels first, and the Python rules stay as the comparison base and for every value a kernel\ndoes not decide, which is where error texts come from.\n\nThe template gains Maybe<T> for a key a record may not have, str_enum! for a closed set of strings,\nthe exact_* readers of a kernel's inputs, kernel_first for a rule other modules call as a plain\nfunction, and shadow_kit.py with one file per shadow.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
